# 18. ACCESSIBILITY AND INTERACTION QUALITY

Ensure the redesigned interface remains usable with touch, keyboard, and assistive technology.

Requirements:

- Use semantic buttons for actions.
- Provide accessible names for icon-only controls.
- Maintain visible keyboard focus.
- Do not rely on color alone to communicate status.
- Maintain sufficient text contrast.
- Prefer touch targets of at least 44 × 44 CSS pixels.
- Ensure dialogs have accessible headings and appropriate focus management.
- Keep disabled actions distinguishable from active actions.
- Prevent text clipping in English and Amharic.
- Respect reduced-motion preferences where animations are introduced.
- Keep loading and error messages understandable.
- Preserve existing screen-reader support where present.

For the favorite control, expose its current selected state.

For order tracking, expose status text that communicates the current stage.

For the meal window, show an explicit status label rather than relying on a colored dot.

