# 19. REDUCE NESTED CONTAINERS

One of the main problems with the current interface is excessive card nesting.

The redesign must address this directly.

Avoid structures such as:

- A large dashboard card containing a meal-status card.
- A meal-status card containing separate cards for every piece of metadata.
- An order card containing another status card, timeline card, and pickup card.
- A profile card containing several unnecessary nested profile cards.

Use a simpler visual hierarchy.

Prefer:

- Page sections.
- Section headings.
- Consistent vertical spacing.
- Thin dividers where useful.
- A small number of meaningful surfaces.
- Compact information rows.
- Simple progress indicators.
- Reusable dish cards.

Use a card when it groups related information or provides meaningful visual emphasis.

Do not use a card simply because the content needs a background.

The result should feel lighter and more spacious even though it uses less screen space.

